WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.930
You certainly have a lot.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.140
- A lot of what?
- Books.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.930
Oh.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:17.570
We may not seem like it,
but we read quite a lot.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:26.220
Uneducated, uninterested
riffraff don't make good soldiers.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:37.620
Do you not read books?

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:45.260
Your file says that before
coming here, you always...

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.980
No, never mind.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:03.590
If it'll make me a good soldier,
I'll read books about vegetables, too.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:20.270
I put the bait on.
Now gently cast the line underhanded-like.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:25.440
Now you sit and wait.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:31.980
In that case, I'll serve
as your legs until then.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.440
Why did you keep these?

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:51.340
One must think clearly
before pulling a trigger.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:56.540
I want you to be the gentle
Claes whenever you put those on.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:03.880
That's not a changeable order...
it's a warm-hearted promise.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:27.580
Amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:42.460
I want to protect you and fulfill
my promise to the only one for me

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:50.200
In a world filled with doubt,
I still can't find the answer

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:57.270
Even so, I continue forward... Why?

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:07.680
If I can change this dream-like
reality with my own two hands,

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:15.160
amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:22.800
I want to protect the only one for me

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:30.570
I swear on my beating heart I will
continue to run until I burn away

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:38.010
Amid the eternal love I feel simply by living,

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:46.150
I want to fulfill my promise

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:57.650
"A Day in the Life of Claes"

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.650
Good morning, Triela.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.640
Good morning, Claes...

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:21.680
I wish I had a mesosiderite...

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.530
Eh?

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:27.060
I suddenly thought of it
while looking at the sky.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:31.190
I've been reading a book
about minerals lately, you see...

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:35.340
You're a real romantic, Claes.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.370
Let's go to the dining hall.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.990
Are you going to the
training grounds today, Triela?

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:56.690
Yeah. I'll be there until night.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.530
You don't seem happy.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:02.800
I have all kinds of concerns of my own...

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.530
What are you doing today, Claes?

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.470
The same as always.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.160
Say, Rico...

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.400
Yeah?

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:38.600
I'm sorry about the
other day. I yelled at you...

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.540
The kaleidoscope is fixed now, so...

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:45.270
You're not mad anymore, Henrietta?

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:47.210
No.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:49.080
That's good.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:53.740
Henrietta. Stay by my side again, okay?

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.330
Have Jean-san buy you one.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.830
Eh?

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:10.160
A mesosiderite.

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:14.930
Oh. No, that's okay.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.510
How come?

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:22.410
You can't simply buy things like that.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.980
What are you buying, Claes?

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.180
Nothing.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.860
You're only going to eat yogurt?

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.090
Yes.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:36.690
Are you not hungry?

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:39.960
This is all I can have today.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:43.860
I'm going to take my time eating it,
so don't worry about me.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:12.550
Huh? All the food...

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:18.090
It's already been taken away.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.060
It won't be too long until lunch.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:35.050
Beatrice. I do have
some cookies in my room.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:36.250
Eh?

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:39.190
You'll have to do some work for me, though.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.260
What is this?

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:46.590
A vegetable garden.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:51.190
Weeds... you can eat?

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:55.140
Herbs.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:08:01.840
Parsley, sage, rosemary...
Have you ever heard "Scarborough Fair"?

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.940
No.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:15.610
Hello, Dr. Bergonzi.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:20.050
Oh, Claes. I appreciate
your help again today.

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:35.840
We're going to do some color
dopplers of your heart today.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.840
Okay.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:41.110
You seem exhausted, Doctor.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:45.310
Sorry about my unsightliness.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:49.150
There's an academic conference next month.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:53.020
The European Cardiovascular Conference.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:54.820
I appreciate all your help.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:57.630
I think I can write a
good paper thanks to you.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:01.290
It is my job.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:27.520
Doctor. Do you know "Scarborough Fair"?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:31.490
Yeah. The strange, thought-provoking song.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:38.100
"Find me an acre of land..."

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:42.810
"Plough it with a lamb's horn..."

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:47.440
"And sow it all over with one peppercorn..."

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:52.380
"And then you'll be a true love of mine..."

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:56.550
What do you suppose that means?

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:35.820
Are your tests progressing without trouble?

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:37.120
Yes.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:42.560
How is your daily life lately?
Is there anything you need?

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:45.960
No, I have more than enough.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:49.830
I've been given permission
to grow a vegetable garden,

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:56.000
I can leave my room at my leisure,
and I can play the piano.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.970
Every day is full and complete.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:21.130
That piano...

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:22.800
Eh?

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:28.470
It's always been here.
Long before the agency was even formed.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:30.640
Is that so?

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:35.510
1000 years ago, there was only
a monastery and some fields here.

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:38.380
Later on, an aristocrat built a villa here,

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:41.680
and the government started
using it at the start of the 20th century,

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:46.090
and now it's used as
our agency's main facility.

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:53.030
Then I'm growing herbs on
land that monks cultivated?

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:54.930
Pretty much.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:49.740
What's wrong, Claes?

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.290
Jean-san.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:58.890
Are you ever sad, but
the tears won't come out?

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.330
Yes. It happens.

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:07.370
That's how I feel right now.

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:13.170
My heart feels so full of tears,
but they just won't come out.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:19.610
Instead, they quietly
spill out when I'm sleeping.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:35.790
I feel like I've been here before...

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.900
Hey.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:54.920
Cyborgs need to be with their
Handlers to use the shooting range.

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:59.380
Umm, I just came to look around...

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:02.660
You're Captain Ravalo's...

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.090
Eh?

00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:09.930
You used to come here all
the time, with that GIS hat on.

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:12.730
You used a VP.

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:16.930
You're dressed differently,
so I didn't recognize you.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.110
Nice, Henrietta!

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:01.950
How many shots left?

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:03.150
Three.

00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:05.280
Very good!

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:09.260
Claes!

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:10.920
Hello...

00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:14.400
What are you doing here, Claes?

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:19.060
I was just passing by,
so I thought I'd look around.

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:23.070
Henrietta.

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:24.240
Yes, sir?

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:27.440
Remove the magazine
and empty the chamber.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.280
Let's call it a day.

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:32.110
Understood, Giuse-san!

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:39.990
I'm sorry for interrupting you.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:45.290
No, don't worry about it.
Just don't step past the white line.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.420
Yes, sir.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:59.940
I'm not sure why, but
this is a familiar smell...

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:49.950
Claes! What are you doing way out here?

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:53.250
Uh, well...

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:58.930
Are you headed back to the dorms?

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:00.370
Yes.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:01.970
Then hop on!

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:03.070
Eh?

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:05.540
It's a long way to the dorms!

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.780
Ange, you sit in front. Claes, you sit in back.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:13.740
- Get off for a moment, Ange.
- Yes, Priscilla-chan...

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:16.740
I'm riding with two pretty girls!

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:48.320
"Tell him to plough it with a lamb's horn"

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:52.220
"and sow it all over with one peppercorn."

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:57.230
"And then you'll be a true love of mine..."

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:59.930
"Tell him to reap it with a sickle of leather"

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:03.990
"and gather it up with a rope made of heather."

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:16.240
"For then he'll be a true love of mine"

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:20.150
"If you say that you can't, then I shall reply"

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:24.320
"Parsley, sage, rosemary, and thyme..."

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:29.260
"Oh, let me know that at least you will try..."

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:31.160
I'm home...

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:33.230
Welcome back.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:35.930
What did you do today?

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:40.470
The same as always.
Cultivated some herbs, played the piano...

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:43.030
Oh.

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:46.770
Claes! Do I smell gunpowder on you?

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:54.140
Are you sure that smell
isn't coming from you?

00:20:56.680 --> 00:21:00.450
Oh, right!

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:13.070
Well, good night, Claes.

00:21:13.070 --> 00:21:15.370
Good night.

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:29.650
What will you do when they grow?

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:32.220
I haven't thought about it.

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:35.850
I think maybe I'll try an herbal bath.

00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:58.850
What is it?

00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:02.780
I don't know. It might
be some kind of mineral.

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:04.990
Oh.

00:22:04.990 --> 00:22:09.690
Say. Have you ever heard of mesosiderites?

00:22:09.690 --> 00:22:10.930
No.

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:19.590
They're asteroid rocks that fell to
Earth long ago and are still here.

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:25.210
Isn't that just enchanting?

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:28.340
Do you have fun doing this every day?

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:32.150
Yes. Is that hard to understand?

00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:36.550
I don't really know what fun is like.

00:22:36.550 --> 00:22:42.920
Even at work or in the dorms,
I never feel moved or smile.

00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:46.590
Why is it you can have fun, Claes?

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:58.270
I guess someone must've
taught me how long ago.

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:15.620
Are you going to Scarborough Fair?

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:24.670
Parsley, sage, rosemary, and thyme

00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:32.370
Remember me to one who lives there

00:23:32.370 --> 00:23:41.770
She once was a true love of mine

00:23:42.420 --> 00:23:50.160
Tell her to make me a cambric shirt

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:57.620
Parsley, sage, rosemary, and thyme

00:23:59.270 --> 00:24:06.980
Without no seams nor needlework

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:14.110
Then she'll be a true love of mine

00:24:17.020 --> 00:24:24.690
Tell her to find me an acre of land

00:24:24.690 --> 00:24:32.330
Parsley, sage, rosemary, and thyme

00:24:33.840 --> 00:24:41.540
Between the salt water and the sea strand

00:24:41.540 --> 00:24:50.180
Then she'll be a true love of mine

00:25:01.990 --> 00:25:07.010
"Clever Snake, Simple Pigeon"
